Compared against Proos-Zalka 2003, Kaye-Zalka 2004, and pre-2017 estimates.

## 7. Conclusion

ECDLP-Shor is asymptotically less expensive than RSA-factoring-Shor at
comparable classical security. Concrete numbers make the case that a
future large-scale fault-tolerant quantum computer would break ECC-256 with
\(\sim 10^{11}\) logical Toffoli gates on \(\sim 2300\) logical qubits.

